session:pr672Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #519's title said sh:SPARQLConstraintComponent, but fetching the actual normative W3C SHACL spec text (via curl + section-anchor extraction, since a plain WebFetch kept truncating the ~500KB single-page doc before reaching §6) showed the real type is the generic sh:ConstraintComponent — SPARQLConstraintComponent is an unrelated, already-used constant for the simpler §5.1 sh:sparql mechanism from #54. Rather than trust the issue title, I corrected the plan doc and implementation to match spec. Custom-component validators (ASK per value-node, SELECT with $PATH textual substitution) were built as a new custom_components.rs module reusing sparql_constraints.rs's execution plumbing (parse/run_select/run_ask, made pub(crate)) rather than a parallel Datalog-rule translation, since the queries are arbitrary SPARQL — mirroring the existing split between translate.rs (Core, Datalog) and sparql_constraints.rs (SPARQL-based, direct evaluation). Testing the spec's own worked example (sh:PatternConstraintComponent's IF(bound($flags), ...)) surfaced a genuine, orthogonal sparql_parser bug: BOUND/REGEX/ISBLANK/etc. are only wired into the boolean-FILTER dispatcher, not the value-producing one IF()/COALESCE() use, so they silently evaluate to unbound inside IF(). Rewrote the test fixture with an equivalent &&/|| formulation and filed #674 rather than fixing sparql_parser inside this PR (out of scope, separate crate). CI also flagged a pre-existing, main-also-failing Security Audit job (RUSTSEC-2026-0285, rustls) unrelated to this change — confirmed by watching main's own concurrent CI run fail identically — filed as #677 rather than bumping dependencies here." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:672 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr672Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr672 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr672Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Attach sh:ConstraintComponent invocations to already-parsed ParsedShape/ParsedPropShape via a post-processing pass (attach_component_invocations, called once from parse_shapes) rather than threading a `components: &[ConstraintComponentDef]` parameter through parse_one_shape/parse_property_shapes." ;
    agp:alternative "Threading components through parse_one_shape's own signature was considered first (matches how other per-shape data is built), but parse_one_shape is also called ad hoc by evaluate::shape_conforms_for_node to re-parse an inner shape referenced by sh:not/sh:and/sh:or/sh:node/sh:xone at evaluation time. Changing its signature would have forced a decision about whether custom components apply inside nested inner-shape references too — a materially bigger scope than this issue, and inconsistent with the existing precedent that #54's sh:sparql constraints are never evaluated for inner shapes either. The post-processing pass keeps parse_one_shape's signature untouched, so nested-shape scope stays out of scope exactly as it already was for sh:sparql, without a signature change forcing the question." .
